    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"Precambrian deposits and occurrences that contain base and precious metals, tungsten, and other metals are widely distributed in Colorado--in the Park, Front, and Sawatch Ranges, in the Wet Mountains, and in the Salida, Gunnison, and San Juan regions.  These deposits and occurrences have been divided into six different types on the basis of geologic criteria, and are shown with different symbols on maps plotted using data and plot files on this disk.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
